# 47. Canonical Agent-to-Artemis Evidence Contract

Artemis must not consume raw internal service objects, arbitrary JSON,
frontend display models or Agent-specific undocumented payloads.

One canonical, versioned Agent-to-Artemis contract must exist.

The first implementation or major redesign of this shared contract is a
Shared Foundation Work Package and requires explicit approval.

After it is frozen, every Agent must consume or adapt to that owner.

Do not create one incompatible Artemis schema per Agent.

## 47.1 Canonical Evidence Envelope

The canonical envelope must support, where applicable:

- schemaVersion
- contractVersion
- agentId
- agentRole
- authorityClass
- runId
- correlationId
- decisionContextId
- user or tenant ownership where applicable
- provider or venue
- market type
- symbol
- base asset
- quote asset
- timeframe
- analysis horizon
- analysis timestamp
- source timestamp
- source-candle timestamp
- expiry timestamp where applicable
- freshness status
- freshness reason
- provenance
- data-quality status
- availability
- unavailable reason
- lifecycle status
- signal or conclusion
- direction
- regime
- strength
- confidence value when valid
- confidence method
- confidence provenance
- supporting evidence
- conflicting evidence
- invalidating conditions
- risk flags
- limitations
- recommended next action class
- execution class
- model or algorithm version
- configuration version
- code implementation version
- created and completed timestamps

Fields that do not apply must be omitted or explicitly unavailable according to
the contract.

Do not fill non-applicable fields with fake zeroes, empty success or guessed
values.

## 47.2 Evidence Item

Each supporting or conflicting evidence item should identify:

- evidenceId
- evidenceType
- canonical source
- value and unit when applicable
- interpretation
- directional contribution
- strength or severity when valid
- timestamp
- freshness
- provenance
- quality
- limitation
- correlation family
- explanation key

Raw internal reason codes must not be exposed as final user prose.

## 47.3 Confidence

Confidence is allowed only when:

- The meaning is defined
- The calculation or model is documented
- Inputs are known
- Calibration or evaluation exists when predictive meaning is claimed
- The value is reproducible
- The provenance is recorded

Do not use the same field for:

- Trend strength
- Prediction probability
- Data quality
- Model accuracy
- Agreement count
- Execution feasibility

When confidence is not defensible, return unavailable.

## 47.4 Contract Versioning

Contract changes must be:

- Versioned
- Backward compatible where practical
- Consumer-aware
- Covered by provider and consumer contract tests
- Recorded in the Evidence Ledger

A breaking contract change requires:

- Affected Agent list
- Artemis consumer impact
- Migration or adapter plan
- Rollback
- Explicit approval

